    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0735" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg729"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Saurma to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In compliance with my
                    instructions I have the honor to respectfully transmit for the information of
                    your excellency the inclosed copy of a report of the imperial consul at Apia,
                    dated September 3 last, in regard to the condition of affairs in Samoa.</p>
                <p>The contents of the report reawaken the Imperial Government’s <pb facs="0736"
                        n="730" xml:id="pg730"/> apprehension that under existing circumstances the
                    peace concluded with the rebels will afford no assurance of the lasting
                    restoration of tranquillity in the islands.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Saurma.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d774-a1.xml" xpointer="d774-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
